          ":question/id": "d6a42f32-3ff1-5799-9155-413fd42c36ff",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74043",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ -5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 11{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+11{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & \u2194{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(1)=1\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=1$  into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(3)+3(1)=2\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=5.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=5$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=1,$ which means \n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=5+3+1=9.\n$$"
        }
